2025-04-18 08:57:06,633 - security_agent - INFO - Received response from Heroku AI: {'response': '# Network Security Monitoring Analysis\n\n## 1. Security Implications\n\nNetwork security monitoring focused on unusual protocol usage, large data transfers, DNS tunneling, and suspicious encrypted traffic addresses several critical security concerns:\n\n• **Data Exfiltration**: Adversaries often use these techniques to steal sensitive information while evading detection\n• **Command and Control (C2) Communications**: Attackers establish covert channels using these methods to maintain persistence and control compromised systems\n• **Lateral Movement**: These techniques can indicate attackers moving through the network after initial compromise\n• **Policy Violations**: Even if not malicious, these behaviors may indicate employees bypassing security controls\n• **Zero-Day Exploit Activity**: Novel attacks often exhibit unusual network patterns before signatures are available\n\n## 2. Specific Indicators to Monitor\n\n### Unusual Protocol Usage\n• Applications using non-standard ports (e.g., SSH running on port 8080)\n• HTTP traffic on non-HTTP ports\n• Protocols appearing in unexpected network segments\n• Sudden appearance of rarely used protocols (ICMP tunneling, etc.)\n• Protocol behavior that deviates from standards (abnormal handshakes)\n\n### Large Data Transfers\n• Sudden spikes in outbound traffic volume to external destinations\n• Consistent data transfers occurring at unusual times\n• Disproportionate upload/download ratios\n• Transfers to geographic locations with no business relationship\n• Repeated transfers just below alerting thresholds (threshold hopping)\n\n### DNS Tunneling\n• Abnormally large DNS queries or responses\n• High volume of DNS queries from a single host\n• Unusual DNS record types (TXT, NULL, etc.)\n• Excessive subdomains in queries\n• High entropy in domain names (randomized/encoded characters)\n• DNS queries to newly registered domains\n\n### Encrypted Traffic Analysis\n• TLS connections to low-reputation domains or IP addresses\n• Unusual TLS/SSL certificate characteristics\n• JA3/JA3S fingerprints associated with malware\n• Encrypted traffic patterns inconsistent with the purported application\n• Encrypted connections to countries without business justification\n\n## 3. Investigation Steps\n\n1. **Initial Triage**:\n   • Establish a baseline of normal network behavior\n   • Correlate alerts with other security events\n   • Determine affected systems and potential impact\n\n2. **Evidence Collection**:\n   • Capture full packet captures (PCAP) of suspicious traffic\n   • Collect relevant logs from endpoints, proxies, and firewalls\n   • Extract metadata from encrypted connections\n\n3. **Traffic Analysis**:\n   • Decode and inspect protocol content where possible\n   • Analyze traffic patterns, timing, and volume\n   • Perform DNS query analysis and domain reputation checks\n   • Review historical traffic to identify when behavior began\n\n4. **Endpoint Investigation**:\n   • Identify processes responsible for the traffic\n   • Check for unauthorized or unusual applications\n   • Examine file system for recently modified files\n   • Review user activity and authentication logs\n\n5. **Threat Intelligence Correlation**:\n   • Compare findings against known IOCs\n   • Check destination IPs/domains against threat feeds\n   • Analyze file hashes and network artifacts\n\n## 4. Mitigation Strategies\n\n• **Immediate Containment**:\n  - Implement temporary firewall blocks for suspicious destinations\n  - Isolate affected systems from the network\n  - Terminate suspicious processes and connections\n\n• **Technical Controls**:\n  - Deploy application whitelisting to prevent unauthorized software\n  - Implement DNS filtering and monitoring solutions\n  - Enforce TLS inspection for high-risk traffic categories\n  - Configure data loss prevention (DLP) systems\n\n• **Policy Enforcement**:\n  - Review and update acceptable use policies\n  - Implement strict protocol restrictions by network segment\n  - Establish data transfer limits and approval processes\n  - Enforce encryption standards for all sensitive communications\n\n## 5. Security Controls to Implement\n\n• **Detection Controls**:\n  - Network Traffic Analysis (NTA) systems\n  - Next-generation firewalls with deep packet inspection\n  - DNS monitoring and filtering solutions\n  - NetFlow/IPFIX collection and analysis\n  - Encrypted traffic analysis tools\n  - SIEM correlation rules for the indicators mentioned above\n\n• **Preventive Controls**:\n  - Egress filtering and proxy enforcement\n  - Application-layer firewalls\n  - Network segmentation and zero trust architecture\n  - Protocol whitelisting by network zone\n  - Data classification'}
