2025-04-18 11:47:04,829 - security_agent - INFO - Received response from Heroku AI: {'response': '# Network Security Monitoring Analysis\n\n## 1. Security Implications\n\n* **Unusual Protocol Usage**: \n  - May indicate command and control (C2) communications or data exfiltration attempts\n  - Attackers often leverage uncommon protocols to evade detection\n  - Can represent attempts to bypass firewall rules or signature-based detection\n\n* **Large Data Transfers to Unknown Destinations**:\n  - Potential data exfiltration or unauthorized data sharing\n  - Could indicate compromised systems or insider threats\n  - May represent initial stages of ransomware preparation (data staging)\n\n* **DNS Tunneling**:\n  - Bypasses traditional security controls by hiding malicious traffic within DNS queries\n  - Enables data exfiltration through a normally allowed protocol\n  - Provides covert command and control channels for malware\n\n* **Encrypted Traffic to Uncommon Destinations**:\n  - Helps attackers hide malicious activities from inspection\n  - Could indicate connections to newly established criminal infrastructure\n  - May represent attempts to bypass SSL/TLS inspection mechanisms\n\n## 2. Specific Indicators to Monitor\n\n* **Unusual Protocol Indicators**:\n  - Non-standard ports for common protocols (e.g., HTTP not on port 80/443)\n  - Unexpected protocol behavior patterns\n  - Protocol anomalies or violations of RFC standards\n  - Use of rarely seen protocols within your environment\n\n* **Large Data Transfer Indicators**:\n  - Sudden spikes in outbound traffic volume\n  - Consistent data uploads during off-hours\n  - Unusual upload:download ratios for specific hosts\n  - Large transfers to new or geographically unusual destinations\n\n* **DNS Tunneling Indicators**:\n  - Abnormally large DNS queries or responses\n  - High frequency of DNS queries from a single host\n  - Unusually long subdomain names (encoding data)\n  - DNS queries containing encoded characters or high entropy strings\n\n* **Suspicious Encrypted Traffic Indicators**:\n  - TLS connections to newly registered domains\n  - Encrypted sessions to IP addresses with poor reputation\n  - Unusual TLS cipher suites or certificate characteristics\n  - Encrypted connections to countries or regions irrelevant to business\n\n## 3. Investigation Steps\n\n1. **Initial Triage**:\n   * Identify affected systems and scope of activity\n   * Correlate suspicious activities across multiple data sources\n   * Establish timeline of events\n\n2. **Deep Analysis**:\n   * Capture and analyze full packet captures when possible\n   * Examine relevant logs (firewall, proxy, endpoint, authentication)\n   * Review historical network behavior for comparison\n\n3. **Context Development**:\n   * Check reputation of external IPs/domains\n   * Validate if connections relate to legitimate business functions\n   * Interview system owners if unexplained activity appears legitimate\n\n4. **Threat Hunting**:\n   * Search for related indicators across environment\n   * Check for persistence mechanisms on affected systems\n   * Analyze lateral movement attempts from suspect systems\n\n## 4. Mitigation Strategies\n\n* **Immediate Response Actions**:\n  - Isolate affected systems if malicious activity confirmed\n  - Block identified malicious destinations at firewall/proxy\n  - Update detection signatures based on discovered TTPs\n\n* **Tactical Improvements**:\n  - Implement stricter egress filtering\n  - Deploy enhanced monitoring for identified weak points\n  - Conduct focused vulnerability assessments\n\n* **Strategic Enhancements**:\n  - Implement zero trust network architecture principles\n  - Develop/update baseline of normal network behavior\n  - Improve network segmentation and access controls\n\n## 5. Relevant Security Controls\n\n* **Technical Controls**:\n  - Next-generation firewalls with application awareness\n  - Network traffic analysis (NTA) tools\n  - DNS filtering solutions with analytics capabilities\n  - SSL/TLS inspection for high-risk traffic\n  - SIEM integration with network telemetry\n  - Endpoint detection and response (EDR) solutions\n\n* **Administrative Controls**:\n  - Regular review of network security monitoring alerts\n  - Updated network traffic baselines and profiles\n  - Documented investigation procedures for security events\n  - Regular threat hunting exercises based on current TTPs\n\n* **Preventive Controls**:\n  - Data loss prevention (DLP) solutions\n  - Strict network segmentation policies\n  - Allowlist-based network access\n  - Regular security awareness training on data handling\n\n* **Compliance Controls**:\n  - Regular audits of network traffic patterns\n  - Documentation of security monitoring capabilities\n  - Periodic testing of detection capabilities\n  - Response time metrics for security alerts'}
